1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,878
The reactivity series lists elements from most to least reactive.

2
00:00:03,878 --> 00:00:07,932
Potassium reacts violently even with cold water, iron reacts slowly,

3
00:00:07,932 --> 00:00:14,218
and gold is so unreactive it won't even react with acids. That's why gold and silver jewellery stays shiny.

4
00:00:15,277 --> 00:00:19,566
A metal's reactivity depends on how easily it loses its outer electrons.

5
00:00:19,566 --> 00:00:23,502
Potassium is more reactive than sodium because it has more shells,

6
00:00:23,502 --> 00:00:27,556
so its outer electron is further from the nucleus and easier to lose.

7
00:00:28,615 --> 00:00:33,198
In a displacement reaction, a more reactive element displaces, or pushes out,

8
00:00:33,198 --> 00:00:39,308
a less reactive element from its compound. If A is more reactive than B, then A plus BC gives AC plus B.

9
00:00:40,367 --> 00:00:45,008
Drop copper into silver nitrate solution. Copper is more reactive than silver,

10
00:00:45,008 --> 00:00:50,708
so it displaces it: the solution turns blue as copper nitrate forms, and silver crystals appear.

11
00:00:50,708 --> 00:00:55,702
Put silver into copper nitrate, and nothing happens, because silver is less reactive.

12
00:00:56,760 --> 00:01:00,050
Hang a clean iron nail in blue copper sulfate solution.

13
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:05,750
A brown coating of copper forms on the nail, and the solution turns green as iron sulfate forms.

14
00:01:05,750 --> 00:01:08,452
Iron is above copper in the reactivity series.

15
00:01:09,511 --> 00:01:15,210
Displacement reactions are useful. In thermite welding, aluminium powder reacts with iron oxide.

16
00:01:15,210 --> 00:01:20,792
Aluminium is more reactive, so it takes the oxygen, producing aluminium oxide and molten iron,

17
00:01:20,792 --> 00:01:22,848
which welds railway rails together.

18
00:01:23,907 --> 00:01:28,548
We can predict reactions with the reactivity series. Zinc in calcium chloride?

19
00:01:28,548 --> 00:01:34,012
No reaction: calcium is more reactive. Magnesium in copper sulfate? Yes: magnesium is higher.

20
00:01:35,071 --> 00:01:40,946
Displacement reactions are used in industry and to clean up the environment. Here are four examples.

21
00:01:42,005 --> 00:01:45,706
In thermite welding, aluminium displaces iron from iron oxide.

22
00:01:45,706 --> 00:01:50,583
The reaction is so hot that the iron is molten and fills the gap between two rails.

23
00:01:51,642 --> 00:01:54,756
Waste solutions from mines contain copper compounds.

24
00:01:54,756 --> 00:01:59,103
Adding scrap iron displaces the copper, so it can be collected and reused.

25
00:02:00,162 --> 00:02:02,865
Factory waste water can contain toxic metals.

26
00:02:02,865 --> 00:02:07,447
A more reactive metal displaces them so they can be filtered out of the water.

27
00:02:08,506 --> 00:02:13,324
Jewellers know that gold and silver are near the bottom of the reactivity series,

28
00:02:13,324 --> 00:02:15,850
so they are not attacked by most solutions.

29
00:02:16,909 --> 00:02:20,846
In each case, a more reactive metal displaces a less reactive one.

30
00:02:20,846 --> 00:02:24,547
Pause and predict: will copper displace iron from iron sulfate?

31
00:02:25,606 --> 00:02:31,070
Now it is your turn to shine! Pause the video after each question and try to answer it first.

32
00:02:32,129 --> 00:02:37,475
Question 1: What are the substances at the start of a reaction called? Pause the video now.

33
00:02:38,534 --> 00:02:39,591
Answer: Reactants.

34
00:02:40,650 --> 00:02:44,469
Question 2: What is a displacement reaction? Pause the video now.

35
00:02:45,528 --> 00:02:50,169
Answer: A more reactive element pushes a less reactive one out of its compound.

36
00:02:51,228 --> 00:02:56,222
Question 3: Will silver react with copper nitrate solution? Why? Pause the video now.

37
00:02:57,281 --> 00:03:00,101
Answer: No, silver is less reactive than copper.

38
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:06,095
Question 4: Why does an iron nail turn brown in copper sulfate? Pause the video now.

39
00:03:07,154 --> 00:03:10,209
Answer: Iron displaces copper, which coats the nail.
